The fix for crbug 576427407 (restricted: "[WebAudio] Validate renderSizeHint
without sampleRate"), chromium/src main commit
353c02f83930ccc67f0013c701f69080541821cc (main@{#1744831}), merged to the 159
branch as c1b0e0032eaedd77fa8db9983022d2e162dcb21f (refs/branch-heads/8154@{#500})
on 2026-11-15. The 158 branch (refs/branch-heads/8127) has the same code and had
no merge of it as of its head fe815692fa (8127@{#1777}, 2026-11-15).

AudioContext's renderSizeHint was only validated when sampleRate was also given,
so a page could make the context allocate buffers sized by an unchecked render
quantum. The fix validates it against the maximum sample rate up front (and
again against the device's actual rate), allocates AudioListenerHandler's arrays
with TryAllocate(), and uninitializes rejected contexts.

This is the main commit without its tests (audio_context_test.cc and the WPT
helper rendersizehint-testing.js), regenerated against 158's files: the same
changes (the hunks only move by a few lines). Drop it once 158 has the merge.

